        "left_title": "SN1 Mechanism (Unimolecular)",
        "left_points": [
          "Kinetics: Rate = k[Substrate], first-order overall.",
          "Carbocation Rearrangement: Occurs via a planar secondary carbocation, which can undergo 1,2-hydride or 1,2-methyl shifts to form a more stable tertiary carbocation if possible.",
          "Stereochemical Outcome: Racemization (formation of a racemic mixture of (R) and (S) enantiomers) due to attack from either face of the planar carbocation, though often with slight retention due to ion-pairing."
        ],
        "right_title": "SN2 Mechanism (Bimolecular)",
        "right_points": [
          "Kinetics: Rate = k[Substrate][Nucleophile], second-order overall.",
          "Carbocation Rearrangement: No carbocation intermediate is formed; thus, no carbocation rearrangements take place.",
          "Stereochemical Outcome: Complete Walden inversion of configuration (e.g., starting with (R)-2-bromobutane yields (S)-butan-2-ol)."
        ],
